b. The tangent curve has period $2\pi$. The line meets two branches in the specified domain.

$\begin{aligned}2\tan\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)&=2\sqrt3\\\tan\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)&=\sqrt3\end{aligned}$

Let $u=\frac{x}{2}$, so $0\le u\le2\pi$.

$\begin{aligned}u&=\frac\pi3,\frac{4\pi}{3}\\x&=2u\\x&=\frac{2\pi}{3},\frac{8\pi}{3}\end{aligned}$

