The graphs meet at the origin and once on each side of it. There are three real solutions, of which one is positive. Outside $[-2,2]$, the line lies beyond the curve's range.

The right-hand side is non-negative. An intersection requires its height to be at most the cosine curve's maximum, $1$.

$\begin{aligned}\left|\frac{x-\pi}{5}\right|&\le1\\|x-\pi|&\le5\\\pi-5&\le x\le\pi+5\end{aligned}$

The V-shaped graph has vertex $(\pi,0)$ and reaches height $1$ at $x=\pi-5$ and $x=\pi+5$.

